{{! spritesheetbelli template
name: Unity (TexturePacker Importer)
extension: tpsheet
per_page: true
rotation: none
layouts: grid, packed

The .tpsheet file of TexturePacker, format 40300, which the free TexturePacker Importer
package reads to cut the PNG next to it into sprites. Unity measures from the bottom
left: y is from the bottom of the page, and the pivot is across the packed pixels from
their bottom left, so a trimmed frame's pivot stays where it was in the whole frame and
can be below 0 or above 1. Frames without a pivot (a grid sheet's while pivots are off
in Settings) turn around their middle. Names escape %, #, : and ; as the importer
expects. There are no borders for 9-slicing, and Unity can't use turned frames.
}}
#
# Sprite sheet data for Unity.
#
# To import these sprites into your Unity project, install the free "TexturePacker Importer":
# https://www.codeandweb.com/texturepacker/unity
#
# Written by {{app}}
#
:format=40300
:texture={{image}}
:size={{image_w}}x{{image_h}}
:pivotpoints=enabled
:borders=disabled

{{#frames}}
{{name | tpsheet-escape}};{{x}};{{image_h | minus y | minus h}};{{w}};{{h}}; {{#has_pivot}}{{pivot_px_x | minus trim_left | divide w | round 6}};{{source_h | minus pivot_px_y | minus trim_bottom | divide h | round 6}}{{/has_pivot}}{{^has_pivot}}0.5;0.5{{/has_pivot}}; 0;0;0;0
{{/frames}}
